Minikube deployment steps:
Deploy flow use docker: !!!NOT UPDATED IMAGE WHEN BUILD IN DOCKER!!!
0.make any changes in app files
docker build -t flask-yaml-image .
minikube image load flask-yaml-image:latest --overwrite
> for first deploy
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
> if you need to re deployed use:
kubectl rollout restart deployment <deploymentname>
> for example deployment name contain in deployment.yaml file
kubectl rollout restart deployment flask-yaml-app
kubectl get pods
kubectl proxy --port=8001


Deploy use minikube only:
minikube image build -t flask-yaml-image .
> for first deploy
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
> if you need to re deployed use:
kubectl rollout restart deployment <deploymentname>
> for example deployment name contain in deployment.yaml file
kubectl rollout restart deployment flask-yaml-app
kubectl get pods
kubectl proxy --port=8001

For Docker users:
build container:
root folder:
docker build -t <myapp-name> .
other folder:
docker build -t test-flask-app ./basic_example

run container:
docker run --rm <myapp-name>
forward a port default for example for Flask:
docker run -p <port>:<port> <myapp-name>
docker run -d -p 50000:50000 test-flask-app

remove container:
get container id:
docker ps
remove:
docker rm -f <container_id_or_name>

remove container image:
get image id or name:
docker images
remove:
docker rmi -f <image_id_or_name>



All camands:
-------------------------------------------
Docker Images:
Show images:
docker images
Delete image:
docker rmi <image_id_or_name>
Force delete image:
docker image rm -f <image_id_or_name>

Docker Containers:
For stop:
docker stop <container_id_or_name>
Forced Kill:
docker kill <container_id_or_name>
Remove:
docker rm <container_id_or_name>